            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0369" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-02T15:00:00-06:00">September 2, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>83. Department’s instruction No. 13, July 21 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >22</hi>],<anchor n="5" xml:id="d258-f1"/> Government of Honduras accepts
                    cooperation American engineers. Have suggested that Minister of Public Works so
                    advise Pan American Union direct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
